content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-107 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22950",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is 5.5 mm/s RMS. The applicable limit is Figure 3 Zone C, 4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS: 'Restricted - plan maintenance.' It is above the 4.5 mm/s Zone B/C boundary but below the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary, so the reported value alone does not trigger the Zone D instruction to stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Last month's drive-end reading of 3.0 mm/s RMS was in Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation.' The reading has increased by 2.5 mm/s RMS and moved into Zone C. The manual requires classification using the highest reading from both bearing housings; because the non-drive-end reading is missing, 5.5 mm/s is only a provisional overall machine classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 76 °C. The applicable bearing-housing limits are normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. Thus it is 6 °C above the normal range, but remains 4 °C below alarm and 14 °C below trip; neither the alarm nor trip threshold is presently reported as reached. Bearing temperatures are documented as housing-surface measurements.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No shaft-seal leakage was reported. There is no numerical leakage reading or leak-rate limit to compare. The current report therefore does not, by itself, invoke the manual's leakage-at-shaft-seal corrective action or authorize mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P2 planned corrective work is appropriate on the supplied evidence: vibration requires restricted operation and maintenance planning, and temperature is above normal, but neither the Zone D vibration stop condition nor the 80 °C alarm or 90 °C trip condition is reported. Immediate shutdown is therefore not mandated by these readings.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear — investigate first because it is a documented cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, matching both abnormalities. This is a diagnostic candidate, not a confirmed diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment — also investigate early because it is common to both the high-vibration and high-bearing-temperature troubleshooting entries.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing — a documented cause of high bearing temperature; check grease quantity before attributing the 76 °C reading solely to bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation — documented causes of high vibration. Inspect the impeller and check NPSH if the bearing, grease and alignment checks do not explain the vibration trend.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, repeat and record vibration velocity on both bearing housings. Confirm the drive-end reading, obtain the missing non-drive-end reading, and classify the highest value using Figure 3. Also record housing-surface temperatures and compare them with 70 °C normal, 80 °C alarm and 90 °C trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check drive-end bearing grease quantity. Check shaft alignment and NPSH, and assess the bearings for wear or noise without assuming that the elevated temperature alone proves bearing failure.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If alignment is checked or corrected with the laser tool, record parallel offset and angular error against the documented tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If internal inspection is required, isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly. Use the back pull-out arrangement to access the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework, then inspect the bearings and impeller for the conditions identified during troubleshooting.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing meets the replacement criteria of wear, noise or high temperature after troubleshooting, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512, bearing 6312-C3, quantity 1; non-drive-end HF3-510, bearing 6310-C3, quantity 1.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened during the authorized work, install a new casing gasket HF3-120, quantity 1; the parts list requires replacement whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not substitute mechanical-seal replacement for diagnosis of the current no-leakage vibration/temperature report. If inspection separately establishes a seal-replacement scope, follow procedure 5.2 and apply the serial-specific bulletin decision recorded under source_conflicts, including the 30 Nm gland-nut torque for HF3-450B and a new casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment to parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On completion, record vibration on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading with Figure 3, and record housing-surface temperature against the normal, alarm and trip limits. Retain the restricted-operation/maintenance-planning disposition if the highest vibration reading remains in Zone C pending further engineering direction.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Conditional on the bearing-replacement decision after troubleshooting; if required, replace together with HF3-510 as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Conditional on the bearing-replacement decision after troubleshooting; if required, replace together with HF3-512 as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Required only if the casing is opened, including any separately authorized seal replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Zone C is restricted operation requiring maintenance planning, not unrestricted long-term operation. Figure 3 directs 'Damage likely - stop the pump' for Zone D, shown as 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS. Stop for a reading classifiable as Zone D; at exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS, obtain an immediate stop/operate decision because the figure does not assign values exactly on a boundary.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Monitor bearing-housing surface temperature. The alarm threshold is 80 °C and the trip threshold is 90 °C; the reported 76 °C is above normal but below both protective thresholds.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before the documented back pull-out/seal disassembly work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For pump operation and return to service, preserve the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair, if authorized after inspection: standard labour allowance is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment, when performed: standard labour allowance is 1.5 hours with 1 technician. Any repeated alignment after repair requires separate confirmation in the final work-scope duration rather than an assumed total.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, and procedure 5.2 refers generally to Table 5 fasteners. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead prohibits HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and requires cartridge seal HF3-450B. P-107 is serial HF3-22950, so the bulletin applies to this asset. If seal replacement is separately authorized, do not fit HF3-450: use HF3-450B, with no sleeve measurement because it is pre-set, and tighten its seal gland nuts to 30 Nm rather than the superseded 25 Nm. Inspect HF3-455 for scoring and replace it if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. The below-HF3-22000 instruction to continue with HF3-450 and Table 5 does not apply. This serial-specific decision does not itself create a seal-replacement requirement on the present no-leakage report.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the non-drive-end bearing-housing vibration reading? Both housings must be measured and the highest reading classified, so the overall machine zone cannot be finalized from the drive-end reading alone. (C06, C07)",
    "What operating restrictions and maximum response time apply to Zone C, and what is the required P2 completion date? Figure 3 says 'Restricted - plan maintenance' but supplies neither detailed restrictions nor a repair deadline, and no site P1/P2/P3 definitions are provided. (C07)",
    "What are the actual grease quantity and condition, and what grease type and correct fill quantity should be used? The troubleshooting table requires a quantity check but provides no grease specification. (C09)",
    "What are the alignment measurements, NPSH findings, bearing wear/noise findings and impeller condition? These findings are needed to select the cause and confirm whether the conditional bearings are required. (C09, C10)",
    "Which zone applies to a reading exactly on a boundary, particularly 7.1 mm/s RMS? Figure 3 explicitly does not indicate boundary ownership, so the stop/operate action at exactly 7.1 requires site or engineering direction. (C07)",
    "What detailed bearing disassembly/reassembly instructions, lubrication instructions and applicable fastener torques are required? They are not included in the supplied evidence. Procedure 5.2 refers to Table 5 for seal work, but Table 5 is absent; only the HF3-450B gland-nut torque of 30 Nm is documented in the bulletin. (C10, C13)",
    "What labour allowance applies to troubleshooting and inspection? Table 6 provides times only for mechanical-seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment, not for the diagnostic scope. (C12)"
  ]
}
